# KNOWN GAP — a DISCARDED `Box.new(...)` LEAKS; the bare `Box(...)` spelling of
# the byte-identical program does not.
#
#     Box(mk("aaaa...","bbbb..."))       -> rc 0, ASan clean
#     Box.new(mk("aaaa...","bbbb..."))   -> rc 1, LeakSanitizer: detected
#                                           memory leaks (the direct 32 bytes
#                                           from `__gorget_box_alloc_GorgetString`)
#
# ⚠⚠ CAUSE -- CORRECTED 2026-08-27 by brief-review pass 13, which BUILT the
# previously-recorded fix and measured it INERT. The original header blamed
# `tag_ownership.rs` for an ownership-tag asymmetry and pointed at
# `heap_alloc_consumer_externs` as the scaffolded fix. BOTH WERE WRONG, and an
# executor following the old header would have implemented a NO-OP.
#
#   (a) INERT: with BOTH tagger arms consulting
#       `Module::heap_alloc_consumer_externs`, this repro is BYTE-IDENTICAL
#       (65 B / 2 allocs) and the GIR still has no `drop_if_alive`.
#       `src/ir/tag_ownership.rs:56-57` says why in its own doc-comment:
#       "Does not introduce drops or registrations -- drop tracking is
#       independent of ownership inference."
#       This is a DROP-TRACKING problem, not an ownership-inference one.
#
#   (b) INVERTED: `Box.new` -- the LEAKER -- travels `Instruction::Call`,
#       which is the arm that HAS the fallback. Bare `Box(` travels
#       `CallExtern` and is CLEAN, because of the explicit
#       `ctx.drops.register_local(dst, ...)` at
#       `src/ir/lowering/exprs/calls.rs:1209-1212`.
#
# Note the path too: the tagger is `src/ir/tag_ownership.rs`, not `src/lir/`.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS THE MIRROR OF `box_trait_bare_ctor_struct_field_uaf.gg`. One root,
# both sides, and they MUST be fixed together:
#     * bare `Box(...)`  REGISTERS and double-frees through the trait pack.
#     * `Box.new(...)`   does NOT register and LEAKS (this fixture).
# The pair is its own positive control. Deleting the bare spelling's
# registration would make the crash go away by converting it into THIS leak --
# a green suite hiding the same defect.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by the wired ASan test): rc 0, no leak, on both backends.
# Measured 2026-08-27 at HEAD by R45 Track A brief-review pass 12;
# orchestrator-verified with `--sanitize` against the bare-spelling control.

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    Box.new(mk("aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa", "bbbbbbbbbbbbbbbb"))
    print(1)
